<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  No-install TableCloth / Windows Sandbox configuration (simplified default, generic launcher)

  Purpose: run TableCloth without installing the host app. Double-click this .wsb and, inside
           Windows Sandbox, a small launcher (SporkBootstrap) is downloaded which then fetches
           the latest portable TableCloth with progress, verifies, extracts and runs it.
           (.wsb is XML: download it in a browser and double-click to start Windows Sandbox.)

  How it works:
    Windows Sandbox runs the LogonCommand with its console window hidden, so the hidden shell
    only spawns one VISIBLE PowerShell window (-WindowStyle Normal). Everything else happens
    inside that window:
    1) Window title / status message (immediate feedback).
    2) DNS pre-correction (probe-then-fallback): only when name resolution fails, fall back to
       public DNS (8.8.8.8 / 1.1.1.1). Working DNS (corporate internal resolvers etc.) is left
       untouched. Chicken-and-egg: the downloads below need DNS, so this single step stays
       inline. Background / opt-out: https://github.com/yourtablecloth/TableCloth/issues/285
    3) Chocolatey-style bootstrap: ensure TLS 1.2, then download the preparation script TEXT
       from the fixed release URL and run it in-session, with no temp file:
         iex ((New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('...tablecloth-prepare.ps1'))
       The script downloads the latest launcher (SporkBootstrap_<arch>.exe) and starts it.
       Byte-level download progress is intentionally OFF here: PowerShell 5.1 progress
       rendering slows the transfer, the launcher is small, and the real progress UX (the
       big TableCloth download) is owned by the launcher GUI. Because the script runs
       in-session, its 'exit' closes this window, so the window disappears by itself once
       preparation finishes.
       (Script source of truth: tools/no-install/tablecloth-prepare.ps1 in the repository.
        Logic changes ship with the next release without redistributing this .wsb.)
    Failures stay visible: both the inline catch below and the script's own catch print the
    error in red and wait for Enter before the window closes (no lingering console otherwise).
    Note: Set-ExecutionPolicy is unnecessary here - the window is started with
    -ExecutionPolicy Bypass, and iex does not consult the execution policy at all.

  Encoding note: keep this file and the preparation script ASCII-only. Windows PowerShell 5.1
  reads BOM-less scripts via the legacy ANSI codepage, WebClient.DownloadString decodes
  charset-less responses (GitHub release assets) the same way, and guest codepages vary by
  host language pack, so non-ASCII display strings get mangled (observed with Korean text).
  Localized user-facing text lives in the launcher GUI, which handles languages at runtime.

  Security:
    - No MappedFolders: zero host file access (structurally blocks exfiltration by a malicious
      .wsb). File-based NPKI certificates cannot enter this environment, so the recommended
      authentication path in this lane is mobile authentication.
    - Trust: controlled HTTPS (official GitHub releases) plus signed launcher / TableCloth
      executables. The preparation script comes from the same origin, adding no new trust surface.
    - Commands / scripts are NOT hidden behind Base64 (-EncodedCommand): encoded PowerShell is a
      classic AV/EDR heuristic flag, and plain-text transparency is part of this file's trust model.

  Note: for parameterization (site preselection deep links, version pinning, offline / private
        mirrors) see docs/PARAMETERIZED_WSB_SPEC.md. This file is the generic-launcher simplified
        default. Fixed-URL assets (tablecloth-prepare.ps1 / SporkBootstrap_<arch>.exe /
        Spork_<arch>_Portable.zip) activate once a release containing them is published.
-->
<Configuration>
  <Networking>Enable</Networking>
  <vGPU>Disable</vGPU>
  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "Start-Process powershell.exe -WindowStyle Normal -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-ExecutionPolicy','Bypass','-Command','$Host.UI.RawUI.WindowTitle = ''TableCloth Setup''; Write-Host '' Getting TableCloth ready...'' -ForegroundColor Cyan; if (-not (Resolve-DnsName -Name github.com -QuickTimeout -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) { Get-NetAdapter | Where-Object Status -eq ''Up'' | Set-DnsClientServerAddress -ServerAddresses 8.8.8.8,1.1.1.1 }; [Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol -bor 3072; try { iex ((New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString(''https://github.com/yourtablecloth/TableCloth/releases/latest/download/tablecloth-prepare.ps1'')) } catch { Write-Host ('' Failed: '' + $_.Exception.Message) -ForegroundColor Red; $null = Read-Host '' Press Enter to close'' }'"</Command>
  </LogonCommand>
</Configuration>
